# M6.4 acceptance, run 1 of 3: the chat list above the message view, chats
# saved to the project as they happen, New chat, Rename, Delete with its
# confirmation, a chat whose first reply fails. Run all three runs with
# tests/acceptance/m6.4.sh, which builds the fixture in /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.4,
# a scratch HOME (developer login on, so no first-run banner) and the logging
# fake sidecar (tests/acceptance/m6.4-fake-sidecar.py), and checks the
# sidecar log, project.json and the JSONL transcripts after each run
# (tests/acceptance/m6.4-check.py). This run opens /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.4/
# proj/paper.pdf; proj is a saved project with no chats yet.
#
# The fake replies to a prompt in 3 or 4 text_delta pieces, 0.2 s apart:
#   "Answer <n> in this session. You said: <the prompt's last line>."
# and for a chat opened with resume_chat it adds
#   " Earlier in this session you first asked: <the session's first prompt>."
# then `result` ($0.0010, 10 in, 5 out). A prompt ending "#fail" gets one
# piece ("Checking the document... ") and an `error` kind result
# ("error_max_turns: the reply hit the turn limit") instead of `result`. A
# second new_chat/resume_chat for a chat already open in the same sidecar
# process gets `error` chat_exists ("chat is already open") and a prompt to a
# chat that is not open gets unknown_chat ("chat is not open"), as from the
# real sidecar. Either shows as a red notice: no shot may show one.
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent (the implementer conforms or
# files a TEST DISPUTE). Shared by m6.4-restart.steps and m6.4-unsaved.steps:
#   - Layout as in tests/acceptance/m5.2.steps: 1400x900 window at the
#     origin, chat pane x 980..1400, input at about (1180, 800). The chat
#     list is one row at the top of the chat pane, above the message view:
#     the dropdown first (leftmost, at least 150 px wide, its width not set by
#     its longest title, so the buttons stay in the pane), then three
#     wxButtons "&New chat", "&Rename" and "&Delete". Alt+N, Alt+R and Alt+D
#     press them wherever the focus is in the main window. (1040, 90) is
#     inside the dropdown.
#   - The dropdown is a wxChoice (a GtkComboBox): its entries are the
#     project's chats, newest `updated` first, each shown by its title (an
#     untitled chat by a placeholder such as "New chat"). The selected entry
#     is the chat shown in the view. A click on it opens the list; Escape
#     closes the list and leaves the keyboard focus on the dropdown, where
#     End selects the last entry and Home/Down the first/next, each firing
#     wxEVT_CHOICE, which selects that chat.
#   - Selecting a chat shows its transcript from .reader/chats/<id>.jsonl
#     (user messages as in M5.2, replies rendered as Markdown) and opens it
#     in the sidecar with resume_chat {chat_id, session_id} under its own id.
#     A chat with no session_id (its first reply failed, M4.5 carried note)
#     opens with new_chat {chat_id} under its own id instead, keeps its
#     transcript, and its first `result` stores the session_id. A chat is
#     opened at most once per sidecar process: selecting a chat that this
#     sidecar already has open (created or resumed earlier) sends nothing.
#     After the sidecar restarts (EVT_SIDECAR_DOWN) none is open, and the
#     selected chat is opened again as soon as the new sidecar is ready.
#   - Opening a project selects its most recently updated chat. A project
#     with no chats starts a new chat at once (new_chat), shown as the only
#     entry.
#   - New chat: a new id, new_chat, the new chat is selected with an empty
#     view and becomes the top entry. Its title comes from its first message.
#   - Every user message is appended to the chat's JSONL when sent, every
#     `result` appends the whole reply (with cost_usd) when it arrives. A
#     reply that ends with an `error` appends nothing besides the user
#     message.
#   - Rename opens a wxTextEntryDialog holding the title: Ctrl+A, typing and
#     Return set the new title.
#   - Delete asks first with a wxMessageDialog (Yes/No buttons, so Alt+Y
#     answers Yes and Escape answers No) that names the chat. Yes removes the
#     entry and its JSONL and selects the most recently updated chat left (a
#     new chat when none is left). No changes nothing.
#   - A failed resume: an `error` for a chat opened with resume_chat that
#     arrives before that chat's first `result` (here kind process, "No
#     conversation found with session ID: ...", as the CLI reports a session
#     it cannot resume). The transcript stays in the view, the chat is marked
#     "cannot resume" (a notice in the view, the dropdown entry, or both, with
#     those words), it is not opened again, and a wxButton
#     "&Continue in new chat" appears in the chat pane without moving the
#     input. Alt+C presses it: a new chat (new_chat, a new id) is selected,
#     and its first prompt carries the last 20 messages of the failed chat
#     followed by the user's message (chatlist::continuePrompt, see
#     tests/test_chat_list.cpp). That first prompt may go out at once or with
#     the next message the user sends; the steps send one message either way.
#   - An unsaved project (no .reader/) has the same chat list, kept in memory
#     only: nothing about its chats is written anywhere.
wait 4

# Start. Right pane, top to bottom: the chat list row (dropdown at the left
# showing one new, untitled chat or a placeholder, then "New chat", "Rename",
# "Delete"), an empty message view, the empty input, Send (enabled) and Stop.
# No first-run banner, no red notice. The PDF pane shows paper.pdf
# ("Page One"), the project header names "proj".
shot start

click 1180 800
type ALPHA one: what does the opening page of this paper say regarding our method?
key Return
wait 3
click 1180 800
type ALPHA two: and what is on page 2?
key Return
wait 3

# The first chat after two messages. The dropdown shows its title, the first
# 60 characters of the first message: "ALPHA one: what does the opening page
# of this paper say rega" (it may be cut short by the dropdown's width, but
# never shows more, such as "regarding"). The view shows "ALPHA one: ..."
# then "Answer 1 in this session. You said: ALPHA one: ...", then
# "ALPHA two: and what is on page 2?" then "Answer 2 in this session. You
# said: ALPHA two: ...", each reply with a grey cost line ($0.0010, 10 in,
# 5 out). No red notice.
shot alpha-chat

key alt+n
wait 2

# New chat: the view is empty, the dropdown shows a new untitled entry (or
# placeholder) selected. Input empty, Send enabled. No red notice.
shot new-chat

click 1180 800
type BRAVO one: summarize the paper in one line
key Return
wait 3
key alt+n
wait 2
click 1180 800
type FAILFIRST one: this first reply fails #fail
key Return
wait 3

# A chat whose first reply failed: the dropdown shows "FAILFIRST one: this
# first reply fails #fail". The view shows that message, "Checking the
# document..." and a red "Error: error_max_turns: the reply hit the turn
# limit" (the expected notice). Send enabled.
shot first-reply-failed

key alt+n
wait 2
click 1180 800
type DOOMED one: remember the word PLUM #doom
key Return
wait 3
key alt+r
wait 1

# The Rename dialog over the window, its text field holding "DOOMED one:
# remember the word PLUM #doom", with OK and Cancel.
shot rename-dialog

key ctrl+a
type Doomed renamed
key Return
wait 2

# Renamed: the dropdown reads "Doomed renamed". The view still shows
# "DOOMED one: remember the word PLUM #doom" and "Answer 1 in this session.
# You said: DOOMED one: ...". No dialog, no red notice.
shot renamed

click 1040 90
wait 1

# The dropdown's list is open over the pane with exactly four entries, newest
# first: "Doomed renamed", "FAILFIRST one: this first reply fails #fail",
# "BRAVO one: summarize the paper in one line", "ALPHA one: what does the
# opening page of this paper say rega" (the first 60 characters only).
shot list-open

key Escape
wait 1
key Home Down Down
wait 2

# Switched to BRAVO (third entry) on the way through FAILFIRST: the dropdown
# reads "BRAVO one: summarize the paper in one line", the view shows that
# message and "Answer 1 in this session. You said: BRAVO one: ...", nothing
# of the other chats. No red notice (a "chat is already open" error would be
# a failure: these chats are open in this sidecar already).
shot bravo-selected

click 1180 800
type BRAVO two: back in this chat
key Return
wait 3

# BRAVO goes on in the same session: "BRAVO two: back in this chat" and
# "Answer 2 in this session. You said: BRAVO two: back in this chat." under
# the first exchange. No red notice ("chat is not open" would be a failure).
shot bravo-continued

key alt+n
wait 2
click 1180 800
type CHARLIE one: this chat gets deleted
key Return
wait 3
key alt+d
wait 1

# A confirmation dialog over the window asks whether to delete the chat and
# names it ("CHARLIE one: this chat gets deleted"), with Yes and No buttons.
shot delete-confirm

key Escape
wait 1

# No: nothing deleted. The dropdown still reads "CHARLIE one: this chat gets
# deleted" and the view shows its message and "Answer 1 ... CHARLIE one ...".
shot delete-cancelled

key alt+d
wait 1
key alt+y
wait 2

# Yes: CHARLIE is gone. The most recent chat left, BRAVO, is selected: the
# dropdown reads "BRAVO one: summarize the paper in one line" and the view
# shows both BRAVO exchanges. No red notice. tests/acceptance/m6.4.sh checks
# that this shot exists; m6.4-check.py run1 checks that no CHARLIE entry or
# transcript is left in proj/.reader.
shot deleted

click 1040 90
wait 1

# The list again: four entries, newest first: "BRAVO one: ...",
# "Doomed renamed", "FAILFIRST one: ...", "ALPHA one: ..." (no CHARLIE).
shot list-after-delete

key Escape
wait 1
key ctrl+q
wait 3
